    "body": "Copy→Add requests previously chose Add immediately or stopped after Copy. This refines the existing shared signed-H4 role and continuation routers so the second Add uses the newly committed Copy record, preserving the lexical emitter and fixed geometry. A nonexecuting provenance witness restores and validates the exact previous artifact; matched controls restore whole previous components. No serving features, proposal rules, templates, matrix products or provider responses are added.\n\nThe first candidate passed new cases but regressed eight historical Repeat queries and was rejected. The accepted retry adds 32 original-parent chain contexts to 527 offline preservation contexts. All candidates, interrupted work and charges are preserved. Offline operator/record labels are declared; complete-response evaluation freely selects operations.\n\nActual construction 36/36, open 24/24, reversed/equal-value 24/24 and post-selection fresh 24/24 pass, including exact pending/committed operands, reads, EOS/checkpoints and independent fresh-record followups. Copied-result exclusion retains the first Copy and stops in every case; parent-router/action/read/geometry controls lose the corresponding behavior. All 663 retained answers and previous panels pass, including both 16-case history-chain populations, 254 transition replays and 72 lexical outputs. Every previously correct historical/action-control row and correctness count is preserved; changed already-incorrect rows remain recorded individually. Native API 117 checks, 22 unique focused tests, kernel source guard, five actual artifact allocation/checkpoint tests and 36 compiled/executed generated Rust equalities pass. Queue statuses are compatibility acknowledgements, not tests.\n\nRetain 2dc63b2c at declared bounded scope. Combined with prior Add→Add/Add→Copy, this meets #1140's stated two-operation, complete-emission and causal-control acceptance. It does not qualify arbitrary wording, general prose/reasoning, Rust program synthesis, alpha or energy savings. New-artifact browser/WASM/HTTP is NOT_RUN. Next #973 diagnostic is complete-sentence requests over retained nonnumeric facts, tracing source identity and shared emission activation.\n\nThis cycle used 2295.009 model seconds; cumulative 16448.361/17250.000 seconds. The 1,800-second and 2 GiB storage extensions were recorded before use; all prior charges and 128 MiB margin are preserved. No unique deletion or paid compute. Exact sources, commands, resources and negative results are bound in docs/evidence/native_geometric_copy_add_1140.json.\n\nCloses #1140\nReferences #973, #820\n",
